\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Overview of the Simulink model \texttt  {SpaceRobot.slx}   This figure shows the Simulink-based closed-loop simulation framework for the free-floating space robot. The model integrates the robot dynamics, reference generation, observation assembly, reward computation, and a PPO-based reinforcement learning agent that outputs joint torques. The reward and termination logic evaluate end-effector tracking performance, base motion disturbance, and control effort to guide policy learning.}}{7}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spacerobot_slx}{{3}{7}{Overview of the Simulink model \texttt {SpaceRobot.slx} \\ This figure shows the Simulink-based closed-loop simulation framework for the free-floating space robot. The model integrates the robot dynamics, reference generation, observation assembly, reward computation, and a PPO-based reinforcement learning agent that outputs joint torques. The reward and termination logic evaluate end-effector tracking performance, base motion disturbance, and control effort to guide policy learning}{figure.caption.4}{}}
\newlabel{fig:spacerobot_slx@cref}{{[figure][3][]3}{[1][5][]7}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Overview of the Robot Subsystem in the Simulink Model \texttt  {SpaceRobot.slx}   This figure depicts the Simulink/Simscape Multibody model of the free-floating space robot, consisting of a floating base and a serial 4-DOF manipulator. Joint torque commands are applied to the revolute joints, while joint positions and velocities are measured and fed back as state variables. The base orientation is represented as a normalized quaternion and compared to a reference to compute the base attitude error.}}{7}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spacerobot_slx_robot}{{4}{7}{Overview of the Robot Subsystem in the Simulink Model \texttt {SpaceRobot.slx} \\ This figure depicts the Simulink/Simscape Multibody model of the free-floating space robot, consisting of a floating base and a serial 4-DOF manipulator. Joint torque commands are applied to the revolute joints, while joint positions and velocities are measured and fed back as state variables. The base orientation is represented as a normalized quaternion and compared to a reference to compute the base attitude error}{figure.caption.6}{}}
\newlabel{fig:spacerobot_slx_robot@cref}{{[figure][4][]4}{[1][6][]7}{}{}{}}
